# Naming: CLI, generated output and OpenAPI

Same rules as `naming.mdc`, which holds the core vocabulary; these names are public API (invariant 14).

- Generated output: `permdock generate` writes a directory (default `src/permdock`) with one file per kind, named after the kind's kebab name (`constants.ts`, `types.ts`, `sql.ts`, `fields.ts`, `zod.ts`, `valibot.ts`, `arktype.ts`, `json-schema.json`, `standard-schema.ts`, `factories.ts`, `messages.json`, `react.ts`, `vue.ts`, `svelte.ts`, `solid.ts`) and no barrel. One camel identifier per resource, `<resource><Thing>` for values and `<Resource><Thing>` for types (`taskItemRow`, `TaskItemRow`, `taskItemFactory`, `taskItemTable`, `<name>Topic`, `<name>Path`). A vocabulary tuple is `<thing>Names` or `permissionKeys` and its union is the singular (`scopeNames`/`ScopeName`, `roleNames`/`RoleName`, `permissionKeys`/`PermissionKey`, `operationNames`/`OperationName`). Hook modules carry no `App` prefix. Row types live in `types.ts` only. Every module starts with `// @generated by permdock generate <kind>@<version> from <policy> sha-256:<digest>; do not edit`. A generate plugin's `name` is kebab, its config factory camel, its file `<name>.<ext>`.
- OpenAPI output: only `x-permdock-*`, registered `x-oai-*` names, and the opt-in `x-badges` hint. Never another party's namespace (`x-scalar-*`, `x-speakeasy-*`, `x-fern-*`, `x-gnap`, gateway namespaces such as `x-amazon-apigateway-*`) and never `targetFormat`. Draft constructs (OpenAPI 3.3 profiles, Overlay 1.2) always ship next to a stable twin with the pin in `x-permdock-catalog.drafts`.
- A field a specification already names keeps the spec's name; add a row to the "Spec names" table on `getting-started/naming.mdx` before adding it.
- CLI flags share better-supabase's vocabulary (`.agents/rules/cli.mdc`): `--out <file>` and `--out-dir <dir>`, `--format` for the renderer (`text`, `json`, `github`, `sarif`) and `--kind` for the document, `--only` and `--ignore` to narrow, `--force` only to overwrite, `--fail-on <severity>`, `--check` and `--dry-run`, `--yes --effects-digest <digest>`, `--db-url-stdin` (then `DATABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_DB_URL`), `--policy` and `--permissions` for modules, `--for` for a skills target. Error `reason` values are snake_case (`unknown_flag`, `confirmation_required`). Never `--strict`, `--write`, `--db`, `--from` for a module, `--format` for a document kind, `--client` for a skills target, or a secret as a flag value: secrets come from a `--<name>-stdin` flag or the environment.
- Renamed identifiers: a renamed public identifier gets a row in `packages/permdock/src/cli/codemod/renames-<version>.ts` (`permdock codemod <version>`), the same `| Old | New |` row in its changeset, and a row in the "Renamed in <version>" section of `getting-started/naming.mdx`; `pnpm docs:drift` checks that the three agree and that no docs page uses an old name.
